# Counter-example: two distinct LOGIC-plane graphemes of the GMN script sharing an IDENTICAL
# gmeow:gmnCodepoints value ("U+22AB") where only ONE carries a gmeow:gmnSigilScope — the
# sigil-scoped collision exemption of lang:GmnGlyphCollisionShape requires BOTH partners to be
# scoped, so the unscoped partner is an unlawful collision (fires lang:GmnGlyphCollision via the
# sh:sparql of lang:GmnGlyphCollisionShape). Both graphemes are otherwise well-formed: grounded
# in the repertoire (lang:hasGrapheme), canonical codepoints (so the codepoint shapes stay
# quiet), no gmeow:gmnConfusableWith edge (so lang:GmnConfusableGlyphShape stays quiet), and each
# carries its measured gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost feed (so lang:GmnScriptGlyphCoverageShape stays
# satisfied and lang:GmnUncostedScriptGlyph stays quiet) — exactly the one unscoped-collision
# finding fires. It is the logic-plane sibling of tests/counter-examples/gmn-glyph-collision.ttl,
# tightened to the one-partner-scoped case the sigil exemption forbids.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/logic/> .

gmeow:gmnScript lang:hasGrapheme ex:gScopedBarTurnstile , ex:gUnscopedBarTurnstile .

ex:gScopedBarTurnstile a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "U+22AB" ;
    gmeow:gmnSigilScope gmeow:gmnSigilLogic ;
    gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost ex:qCostOne .

ex:gUnscopedBarTurnstile a lang:Grapheme ;
    lang:inScript gmeow:gmnScript ;
    gmeow:gmnCodepoints "U+22AB" ;
    gmeow:gmnGlyphTokenCost ex:qCostOne .

ex:qCostOne a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:dimensionless ;
    math:quantityValue 1 .
